The protocol handling, spatial mixer and session logic are carried over from
wolfvoice largely unchanged. What differs in ConfluenceVoice is packaging for
Windows: configuration is read from a TOML file next to the executable instead
of environment variables and hardcoded Unix paths (see src/config.rs), so it
runs like a normal Windows program rather than a system service.

